{
  "id": "subsets",
  "questionId": "subsets",
  "slug": "subsets",
  "title": "Subsets",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Backtracking",
  "patterns": [
    "backtracking"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "grind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "at each element, you either put it in the current subset or you don't - that's a binary choice you can recurse on",
    "keep a running 'current subset' list as you recurse through the indices from left to right",
    "at each index, first record the current subset as one answer, then recurse choosing to include nums[index], then recurse choosing to exclude it",
    "after the 'include' recursive call returns, remove the element you added before trying 'exclude' - that undo step is what makes it backtracking"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to record the empty subset (the state before any element is chosen)",
    "not undoing the append to the current subset after the recursive call returns, corrupting later subsets",
    "appending the same mutable list object to the results instead of a copy of its current contents"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of distinct integers.\n\n**Return every possible subset of the list (the power set), including the empty subset and the full list itself.**\n\nThe subsets can be returned in any order, and the elements within each subset can be in any order.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10",
      "-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000",
      "all integers in nums are distinct"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "single-element list (2 subsets: empty and the element itself)",
      "negative numbers in the list",
      "list with the maximum allowed length, to check for missed or duplicated subsets"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3]",
        "output": "[[], [1], [2], [3], [1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 3], [1, 2, 3]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[], [1], [2], [3], [1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 3], [1, 2, 3]]",
        "explanation": "all 2^3 = 8 subsets of a 3-element set"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [0]",
        "output": "[[], [0]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[], [0]]",
        "explanation": ""
